WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.090
Choosing the right channel: WhatsApp, video calls, Drive and social media.

2
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.790
This is the video for module 2 of Email and Online Communication.

3
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.260
WhatsApp is fast and cheap on data.

4
00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:17.770
Video calls are now normal for interviews and training.

5
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.540
Google Drive lets a team work on one online copy.

6
00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.880
And employers and customers check your social media.

7
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:33.320
Use WhatsApp for speed: quick questions, orders, delivery updates and group news.

8
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:38.960
Use email for anything formal or anything you may need to prove later.

9
00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:50.090
A useful rule: if you would be upset to lose the message, email it, then mention it on WhatsApp. For example, I have just emailed you the quotation for the 50 T-shirts.

10
00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:57.780
WhatsApp Business is a free app for small businesses. Fill in your profile with name, address and hours.

11
00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:03.360
A greeting message goes out automatically when a new customer writes to you.

12
00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:09.770
An away message replies for you outside your working hours, so nobody feels ignored.

13
00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:17.460
Quick replies are saved answers. Type a slash and a shortcut, like price, and your price list is sent.

14
00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:23.390
Labels are colour tags, so you see which orders are new, paid or delivered.

15
00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:38.720
For example, Ada runs a catering business in Abuja. On Friday at 9:40 pm, Kunle asks the price of small chops for 30 people. Her away message replies that she will answer from 8 am.

16
00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:46.710
At 8:05 am she labels the chat New order and types slash price to send her saved list.

17
00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:56.210
She greets him by name and quotes the medium package, approximately 45,000 naira, and asks when and where the event is.

18
00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:09.150
When he replies, she confirms everything in one message: Saturday 20th, delivery to Garki by 11 am, 45,000 naira, 50 percent deposit to confirm.

19
00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:16.040
After payment she changes the label to Paid and emails a simple invoice as a record.

20
00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:27.420
Two habits protect you here. Confirm agreements in writing. And confirm payment in your bank app before delivering, because fake payment screenshots are a common trick.

21
00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:44.540
Before a video call, run this check. Phone charged above 50 percent. Data or Wi-Fi confirmed. Light in front of you, because light behind you turns your face into a shadow. A quiet spot with earphones. App updated and link open.

22
00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:48.540
Prop the phone at eye level, and join two to three minutes early.

23
00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:58.220
During the call, stay muted unless you are speaking. The first time you speak, say your name, for example, This is Bisi from Ogun state.

24
00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:05.160
Use the chat for questions and links without interrupting, and raise your hand in a large meeting.

25
00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:15.180
Free Zoom meetings end after 40 minutes. Free Google Meet group calls end at 60 minutes, so check the limit before a long meeting.

26
00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:20.420
If your video freezes, turn your camera off first. Audio needs far less data.

27
00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:29.670
Drive keeps one online copy that everyone works on. When you share, choose what each person can do. A Viewer can only read.

28
00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:36.720
A Commenter can add comments but cannot change the text. Good for a manager giving feedback.

29
00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.890
An Editor can change, delete and share the file.

30
00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:48.770
And keep anything with names, phone numbers or money figures on Restricted, so only the people you added can open it.

31
00:03:50.020 --> 00:04:04.250
For example, Blessing sells lace in Aba. A commenter says her lace is overpriced. She replies once, calmly, explains her quality and free delivery in Aba, and invites him to message her for a close-up video.

32
00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:17.020
She does not argue, and hides a later insulting comment. Never send payment details in a public comment, and never post other people's children or locations without permission.

33
00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:23.260
Before you post, use the billboard test: would you be comfortable seeing it on a billboard beside your name?

34
00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:41.550
To remember. WhatsApp for speed, email for records. Confirm agreements in writing. On calls, light in front and muted unless speaking. In Drive, choose the right role and keep private files Restricted. And on social media, reply once and calmly.

35
00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:55.180
Your turn. Switch on a greeting and away message. Run a practice call with a friend and ask for honest feedback. Share a Google Doc as Commenter. And tidy one social media profile.

36
00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:57.470
Continue with the lessons below.
